{"title":"2024 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two standard six-sided dice are rolled. What is the probability that the product of the two numbers rolled is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9ab21e1316847deed90f32c31c6d84a076dea08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\   \\frac{3}{36} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\   \\frac{4}{36} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\   \\frac{6}{36} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\   \\frac{8}{36} \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\   \\frac{9}{36} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"450\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can list all of the pairs of rolls and see which ones have integers that multiply to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> representing a possibility where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> was rolled first and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> was rolled second:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31fa6b94e5a84b15c9a080cd52edc749580d90c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69273482bff8727194f6407e55ac1bfa94d9c555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba3e3f9bd99ddc2bf9e6d9244ebf4bfbc3776d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a1acbf245a710398f64953985490d7b1134630b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbb8858b7eefd40608ac2c33f75f1c80b800bc74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5df99ccd1c7c4b384bb2b3a5b9d270c6aa4abf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/a/f7a25c234892fb8a7738bc31e5ccee3bf9ad5afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/5506b58320deb5004bf2ed2f1a5e3e672d6e326e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68a601c8e837eafe7d899c2ba96295b3637daf6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c6f0e4cd615eb4d118bf243be6594935ad3de9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20c86ca1c4b2e0ef486c0cafcf9a2eefffa10421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/f/70f47290d3c991aac723270e49b5415eb82b2cc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d261236ea904095d8d185a456444545b5206013b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea44bd62795a5d84c16a028ff4fb079a5cb8e63f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04fa1d70044a676ae0a28e1476d5192f5cd8496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc1c720139325a2c3491ba41476d225311fcd1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/9492e0ae17ba8045ad2de885400cf91207e83db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/1/281cb98ef359560b94673052664a637c131ec362.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/78561eb59286ee78766fdc37ef35399bf0355e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1924ac42c8e1d1cb79000224acbe2c46d4b22bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7347741cade420c9172f1251847efddfdeb489ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79ad99fd4eff7c80182e09559fe59f36b5844e2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b148ef6cc1c0ce3aebeede22fd06969a213bd5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/190d53edddf17fdf15d88488290c282a150354d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/1/281cb98ef359560b94673052664a637c131ec362.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/78561eb59286ee78766fdc37ef35399bf0355e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1924ac42c8e1d1cb79000224acbe2c46d4b22bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7347741cade420c9172f1251847efddfdeb489ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79ad99fd4eff7c80182e09559fe59f36b5844e2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b148ef6cc1c0ce3aebeede22fd06969a213bd5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/190d53edddf17fdf15d88488290c282a150354d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e5c05123d72c760159fe732b683014c75008c17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/e/53e45c55a387ecd0ff1c5c07aa081bdcd9a7fbbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/1/ba1cf8a9e18c3e06c87c6bb9840782dc4c7828a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf953fb2c072b3fd3f9daad973c7e1ee5fc53aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b6a364920ec84c82c57831adffe0e2ad2b9be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b5a7c6dea205547307d7f8a9f35366c15b819d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/0/5a0994ca0283f051e07f29844f7af73f4624eef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17384a6c2a4aee0ea47051a974ad1cb5967d47f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e936447969453c86785fddfee03c502514fa298f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a6aa4fae2c4e4c29b43f57a15cd214e525e111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/0429617bc1afa148bd90f2912e2e3f0a85c98ec1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0dd1499dbb1ea032542c13537a2ca2f157d4c832.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We can see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> pairs and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/f/70f47290d3c991aac723270e49b5415eb82b2cc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc1c720139325a2c3491ba41476d225311fcd1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7347741cade420c9172f1251847efddfdeb489ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17384a6c2a4aee0ea47051a974ad1cb5967d47f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> all work, which would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pairs. The probability can be found by dividing the number of possibilities that would result in a product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> divided by the total number of possibilities, which would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b2d9aa442c238300c0a9eae81f9328b22b6833e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } \\frac{4}{36}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Faster.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Faster)\">Solution 2 (Faster)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Faster)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since each six-sided die has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities for each roll, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897dd68f9e342665851f9e9b91b87a28d42fc7e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 6 = 36$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" /> possibilities for two rolls.\n</p><p>The prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/0/9c0bb190fb003fcc2a48f8ca029a45f1abd26faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2} \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />. From this, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/3/5438a50c3f962b0f9d16952b07f0fc0f74c75a1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2 + 1)(1 + 1) = 3 \\times 2 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"209\" height=\"20\" /> factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of these don't work because we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/b/86bdf2d50a31479e6e271d7800d7ee5b632597ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\times 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db7ea8973c654bd2a690a031dbec910a3924ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23fb8f559d4996e0afd7ac74872d2fc0c2c7828b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 &gt; 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebef3aefcc33bf397b3656d6db19d7f2c45b823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 - 2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> factors that are actually usable. We could have also listed all of the factors to determine that there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities.\n</p><p>The probability of having two rolls that multiply to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b2d9aa442c238300c0a9eae81f9328b22b6833e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } \\frac{4}{36}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley\">2024 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3 (page do